#: simcontrols.js:32
msgid "Heating of Solution in a Beaker"
msgstr "Heating of Solution in a Beaker"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Drag the tripod towards the burner"
msgstr "Drag the tripod towards the burner"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Drag the wire gauze towards the top of the tripod"
msgstr "Drag the wire gauze towards the top of the tripod"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Drag and drop the wash bottle near the beaker"
msgstr "Drag and drop the wash bottle near the beaker"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Drag the beaker to the top of the wire gauze"
msgstr "Drag the beaker to the top of the wire gauze"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid ""
"Drag the watch glass containing porcelain chips to the top of the beaker"
msgstr ""
"Drag the watch glass containing porcelain chips to the top of the beaker"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Click on the burner switch to turn on flame"
msgstr "Click on the burner switch to turn on flame"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Drag the thermometer to the beaker to measure the temperature"
msgstr "Drag the thermometer to the beaker to measure the temperature"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Click on the burner switch to turn off flame"
msgstr "Click on the burner switch to turn off flame"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Click on the Inference button"
msgstr "Click on the Inference button"

#: simcontrols.js:34
msgid "Click on the Reset button to redo<br> the simulation"
msgstr "Click on the Reset button to redo<br> the simulation"

#: simcontrols.js:35
msgid ""
"Heating a solution, such as water in a beaker, results in an increase in  "
"<br>temperature due to the absorption of energy. This energy input "
"causes<br>the water molecules to gain kinetic energy, leading to faster "
"molecular<br>motion and,consequently, a rise in temperature. The process is "
"essential<br>for various applications, including dissolving solutes,chemical "
"reactions, <br> and general laboratory procedures. Monitoring temperature "
"changes during <br>heating provides valuable information about the thermal "
"properties of the <br>solution and aids in experimental control and analysis."
msgstr ""
"Heating a solution, such as water in a beaker, results in an increase in  "
"<br>temperature due to the absorption of energy. This energy input "
"causes<br>the water molecules to gain kinetic energy, leading to faster "
"molecular<br>motion and,consequently, a rise in temperature. The process is "
"essential<br>for various applications, including dissolving solutes,chemical "
"reactions, <br> and general laboratory procedures. Monitoring temperature "
"changes during <br>heating provides valuable information about the thermal "
"properties of the <br>solution and aids in experimental control and analysis."

